   "srcName": "Teacher's math update, 10/15",
   "source": "Math facts (from the teacher's update)",
   "summary": {
    "text": "Multiplication facts for the ×0, ×1, ×2, ×5 and ×10 tables, one card per fact with a strategy for working it out and a way to check it.",
    "from": "source"
   },
   "why": {
    "text": "Your class has a pop quiz coming: 50 multiplication facts in 3 minutes. That is under four seconds a fact, so the facts have to come from memory, and the strategies are how they get there.",
    "from": "added"
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "text": "Answer every ×0, ×1, ×2, ×5 and ×10 fact from memory.",
     "from": "added"
    },
    {
     "text": "Use a strategy to work out a fact you are not sure of.",
     "from": "added"
    },
    {
     "text": "Check an answer with a fact you know, or with the turn-around.",
     "from": "added"
    }
   ],
   "parentNote": {
    "text": "Built from the teacher's math update about the multiplication facts pop quiz (50 facts in 3 minutes). Her attached flashcards and practice sheet did not reach Drive, so the facts and strategies here are ours, not copies of hers. This part covers 30 facts. Every answer, strategy step and wrong option was computed, not typed. The facts run to 12 × 12; if her sheet stops at 10 × 10, the x11 and x12 facts are extra. The Facts sprint on each card is the pop quiz shape: typed answers against one clock.",
    "from": "added"
   },
   "nextUp": {
    "text": "Flip the cards once, then try a sprint and see which facts it catches.",
    "minutes": 10,
    "from": "added"
   },
   "cards": [
    {
     "id": "c0",
     "term": "Any number × 0",
     "def": "**0.**\n• Zero groups of anything is nothing at all.\n• 9 × 0 = 0, and 0 × 9 = 0.",
     "hint": "No groups, nothing to count.",
     "from": "source"
    },
    {
     "id": "c1",
     "term": "Any number × 1",
     "def": "**The number itself.**\n• One group of 7 is just 7.\n• 1 × 12 = 12.",
     "hint": "One group: nothing changes.",
     "from": "source"
    },
    {
     "id": "c2",
     "term": "Turn-around facts",
     "def": "**Swapping the two numbers does not change the answer.**\n• 3 × 8 = 8 × 3 = 24.\n• So every fact you learn is really two facts.",
     "hint": "Learn one, get its partner free.",
     "from": "source"
    },
    {
     "id": "c3",
     "term": "Checking your answer",
     "def": "**Check with a fact you are sure of, or with the turn-around.**\n• Not sure of 6 × 7? 6 × 6 = 36, plus one more 6 is 42.\n• On a timed quiz, check the ones you hesitated on, not every one.",
     "hint": "Students know the facts and still slip: the check catches the slip.",
     "from": "added"
    },
    {
     "id": "c4",
     "term": "2 × 2",
     "def": "**4**\n• A square fact: the same number twice.\n• Double 2: 2 + 2 = 4.",
     "hint": "Double it.",
     "from": "source"
    },
